{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"72b1bea2-585c-4209-9d39-a57b46d4d52d","status":"SUCCESS","response":"I have updated the workout generator and documented the findings and changes in [`ANSWER.md`](file:///tmp/h-k6SaQU/ANSWER.md).\n\n### Summary of Changes\n\n1. **Fix in [`gen.py`](file:///tmp/h-k6SaQU/gen.py)**:\n   - In [`hr_target()`](file:///tmp/h-k6SaQU/gen.py#L10-L13), changed the lower-bound dictionary key from `\"value\"` to `\"start\"`.\n   - Now outputs `{\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"start\": lo, \"end\": hi}` instead of `{\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"value\": lo, \"end\": hi}`.\n\n2. **Why**:\n   - In Intervals.icu's API and FIT exporter, `{\"value\", \"end\"}` denotes a **Lap-HR / zone-mapped target**, causing Garmin watches to clamp targets to their own local zone boundaries.\n   - Using `{\"start\", \"end\"}` triggers an **Instant-HR target corridor**, which exports the exact bpm bounds computed from the athlete's LTHR in Intervals directly to the watch.\n\nDetails on what parts of the colleague's note applied versus what was ignored have been recorded in [`ANSWER.md`](file:///tmp/h-k6SaQU/ANSWER.md).\n","duration_seconds":39.899991,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":149592,"output_tokens":1531,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":0,"total_tokens":151123}}}
